WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.380
We see a similar tension in modern
controlled environments.

2
00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:07.480
Right now, behavioral labs are running
studies to map the limits of human

3
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.920
cognition under extreme pressure.

4
00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:14.040
To get authentic data, researchers often
rely on deception.

5
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:18.420
They deliberately mislead participants
about the true purpose of the test to

6
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.960
catch their genuine psychological
reactions.

7
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:25.120
In some designs, this means subjecting
individuals to harsh, inescapable

8
00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.800
public critique, intentionally driving up
their heart rates and triggering

9
00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:29.940
severe psychological reactions.

10
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.860
distress. This methodology sits in direct
opposition to the foundational rules

11
00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:38.840
of human research, respect for personal
autonomy, beneficence,

12
00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.720
and the absolute requirement to do no
harm.

13
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:47.100
So we have to ask, at what point does the
value of scientific discovery stop

14
00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:50.080
justifying the intentional infliction of
pain?

15
00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:54.160
Whether it is a known toxic risk to an
infant in an incubator,

16
00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:59.480
a subpoena waiting for an Irish
paramilitary, or a panic attack induced in a

17
00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:03.140
psychology lab, the mechanism of damage is
the same.

18
00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:08.140
Good science requires clean data, but it
also demands that researchers

19
00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:12.720
proactively interrogate their own methods,
ensuring the pursuit of knowledge

20
00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:15.820
never comes at the expense of human
dignity.
